.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt DEADMAN.CGI 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm deadman.cgi
.Nd record pings for deadman
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /var/www/cgi-bin/deadman.cgi
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
records the pings that
.Xr deadman 8
watches.
.Xr slowcgi 8
runs it for
.Xr httpd 8 ,
in httpd's chroot, for URLs of these forms:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa .../ Ns Ar TOKEN
The check whose token is
.Ar TOKEN
has run.
.It Pa .../ Ns Ar TOKEN Ns Pa /start
It has started.
.It Pa .../ Ns Ar TOKEN Ns Pa /fail
It has run and failed.
.El
.Pp
What comes before the token does not matter; the
.Xr httpd.conf 5
location decides which URLs reach
.Nm .
GET, HEAD and POST all work, and any request body is ignored.
.Pp
.Nm
answers 200 when it has recorded a ping, 404 for a token that is not
configured or not a token, and 405 for any other method.
It records a ping by setting the modification time of the matching file in
.Pa /var/www/deadman ,
which
.Xr deadman 8
creates for each configured check, to now.
It creates nothing, writes nothing and reads nothing, it repeats nothing
from the request, and
.Xr pledge 2
and
.Xr unveil 2
confine it to changing those modification times.
The ping directory is not readable by httpd's user, so
.Nm
cannot list the tokens either.
.Pp
It is linked statically, since the chroot has no shared libraries.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/www/cgi-bin/deadman.cgi" -compact
.It Pa /var/www/cgi-bin/deadman.cgi
.It Pa /var/www/deadman/
The ping files, seen from inside the chroot as
.Pa /deadman .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Enable
.Xr slowcgi 8 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# rcctl enable slowcgi
# rcctl start slowcgi
.Ed
.Pp
Then, in
.Xr httpd.conf 5 ,
a server whose ping URLs are
.Pa https://deadman.example.org/ping/ Ns Ar TOKEN :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
server "deadman.example.org" {
	listen on * tls port 443
	tls {
		certificate "/etc/ssl/deadman.example.org.fullchain.pem"
		key "/etc/ssl/private/deadman.example.org.key"
	}
	location "/ping/*" {
		fastcgi socket "/run/slowcgi.sock"
		root "/cgi-bin/deadman.cgi"
	}
	location * {
		block return 404
	}
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr deadman.conf 5 ,
.Xr deadman 8 ,
.Xr httpd 8 ,
.Xr slowcgi 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Joe Abley Aq Mt jabley@strandkip.nl ,
with Claude.
